<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Analysis of Hyperparameter Sensitivity.</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our experiments demonstrate that the verification effectiveness is largely insensitive to hyperparameter choices as shown in Table <a href="#A4.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ D.4 Analysis of Hyperparameter Sensitivity. ‣ Appendix D Supplementary Experiment Results ‣ CITED: A Decision Boundary-Aware Signature for GNNs Towards Model Extraction Defense" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. Across a wide range of settings, including variations in the coefficient distribution and noise level, the ARUC values remain stable with only marginal fluctuations. This robustness indicates that the verification mechanism does not rely on carefully tuned parameters, but instead captures intrinsic differences between surrogate and independent models. Consequently, practitioners can apply the method without exhaustive hyperparameter search, ensuring consistent reliability in practical deployments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>ARUC results under different coefficient settings. Results are reported as mean <math id="A4.T10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> std.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T10.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T10.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T10.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T10.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">coefficient</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T10.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">ARUC<math id="A4.T10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}^{\text{emb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>emb</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{\text{emb}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
